 This is a NextJS starter in Firebase Studio.
 
 To get started, take a look at src/app/page.tsx.
+
+## Media Monitor Malaysia (`/monitor`)
+
+A free, Meltwater-style media monitoring dashboard focused on Malaysian
+local nuance. No paid APIs or keys — it aggregates public RSS feeds
+server-side and analyses them with transparent, rule-based NLP.
+
+**Coverage** — 20+ Malaysian outlets across four languages (The Star, NST,
+Malay Mail, FMT, Malaysiakini, Berita Harian, Harian Metro, Utusan, Kosmo!,
+Astro Awani, Sin Chew, China Press, Oriental Daily, Borneo Post, Daily
+Express Sabah, SAYS, r/malaysia, The Edge, …) plus Google News MY (EN + BM)
+for keyword searches.
+
+**Malaysian nuance**
+- Language detection: Bahasa Malaysia, English, Chinese, Tamil, and
+  "rojak/mixed" for Manglish-register text
+- Sentiment lexicon covering BM (`teruk`, `berjaya`, `rasuah`, `banjir`),
+  Manglish slang (`syok`, `best giler`, `kantoi`, `hampeh`), English and
+  basic Chinese — with BM negation (`tak/bukan/jangan`) and intensifiers
+  (`memang/sangat/gila`)
+- Entity tagging for coalitions/parties (PH, BN, PN, UMNO, PAS, DAP…),
+  agencies with BM/EN aliases (KWSP/EPF, SPRM/MACC), GLCs and brands,
+  all 13 states + KL/Putrajaya/Labuan, and recurring isu semasa
+  (subsidi, SST, banjir, 1MDB, scam…)
+
+**Dashboard** — keyword tracking (saved locally in the browser), sentiment
+timeline, share of voice, language mix, filterable mention feed with
+per-feed health status.
+
+Key paths: `src/lib/monitor/` (sources + NLP), `src/app/api/monitor/`
+(aggregation API), `src/components/monitor/` (dashboard UI).
